  {
   "xml_index": 1,
   "xml_name": "L11_001_A Point Class",
   "display_name": "A Point Class",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>In this lab we build a small <b>drawing program</b> out of classes, step by step, the way real programs are built: a <code>Point</code>, then a <code>Line</code> made of two points, a <code>Triangle</code> made of three points, and a <code>Scene</code> holding many shapes. At the end, your classes will draw a picture.</p>\n<div style=\"margin:6px 0 4px\"><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;border-radius:4px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:140px\"><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;padding:3px 8px;font-weight:600\">class Point</div><div style=\"padding:3px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #c9d3de\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">x, y, color</div></div><div style=\"padding:3px 8px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">move()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">distance_to()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">draw()</div></div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;border-radius:4px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:140px\"><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;padding:3px 8px;font-weight:600\">class Line</div><div style=\"padding:3px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #c9d3de\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">p1, p2 (Points), color</div></div><div style=\"padding:3px 8px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">length()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">midpoint()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">move()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">draw()</div></div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;border-radius:4px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:140px\"><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;padding:3px 8px;font-weight:600\">class Triangle</div><div style=\"padding:3px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #c9d3de\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">a, b, c (Points), color</div></div><div style=\"padding:3px 8px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">perimeter()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">area()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">center()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">move()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">draw()</div></div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;border-radius:4px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:140px\"><div style=\"background:#2b4c7e;color:#fff;padding:3px 8px;font-weight:600\">class Scene</div><div style=\"padding:3px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #c9d3de\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">shapes (a list)</div></div><div style=\"padding:3px 8px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">add()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">move_all()</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">draw()</div></div></div></div><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">the classes we will build; Line, Triangle and Scene are made of other objects</div>\n<p>We start with <code>Point</code>. A point has coordinates <code>x</code> and <code>y</code>, and a colour, given as a string such as <code>\"red\"</code> (default <code>\"black\"</code>).</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the class <code>Point</code> whose constructor takes <code>x</code>, <code>y</code> and an optional <code>color</code> (default <code>\"black\"</code>), stored as attributes with the same names, and whose <code>__str__</code> returns <code>(x, y)</code> (for example <code>(3, 4)</code>).</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>p = Point(3, 4, \"red\")</code>, <code>print(p)</code> prints <code>(3, 4)</code> and <code>p.color</code> is <code>\"red\"</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        # write your code here\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        # write your code here\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "p = Point(3, 4, \"red\")\nprint(p, p.color)",
