    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 2,
   "xml_name": "L11_002_Moving A Point",
   "display_name": "Moving A Point",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A method can change the object's attributes. Moving a point by <code>dx</code> to the right and <code>dy</code> up means adding <code>dx</code> to <code>x</code> and <code>dy</code> to <code>y</code>:</p>\n<div style=\"margin:6px 0 4px\"><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">p : Point</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">x = 1</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">y = 2</div></div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;padding:22px 8px 0 0;color:#8a939c\">p.move(3, -1) &rarr;</div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">p : Point</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">x = 4</div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">y = 1</div></div></div></div><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">the same object, with new coordinates</div>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> the <code>Point</code> class from the previous question is given. Add a method <code>move(dx, dy)</code> that moves the point (changing its <code>x</code> and <code>y</code>). It returns nothing.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>p = Point(1, 2)</code> and <code>p.move(3, -1)</code>, <code>print(p)</code> prints <code>(4, 1)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        # write your code here\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "p = Point(1, 2)\np.move(3, -1)\nprint(p)",
     "stdin": "",
