     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "p = Point(0, 0)\np.move(0, 0)\np.move(-5, 5)\nprint(p)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(-5, 5)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "p = Point(10, 10)\nr = p.move(1, 1)\nprint(p, r)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(11, 11) None",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 3,
   "xml_name": "L11_003_Distance Between Points",
   "display_name": "Distance Between Points",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The distance between two points follows from Pythagoras: <code>((x2 - x1)<b>2 + (y2 - y1)</b>2) <b> 0.5</code>. A method can take </b>another object of the same class** as a parameter:</p>\n<pre>p.distance_to(q)     # inside the method, self is p and other is q</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> add the method <code>distance_to(other)</code> to <code>Point</code>, returning the distance to the point <code>other</code>, rounded to 2 decimal places.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>Point(0, 0).distance_to(Point(3, 4))</code> returns <code>5.0</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        # write your code here\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(Point(0, 0).distance_to(Point(3, 4)))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "5.0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "p = Point(1, 1)\nprint(p.distance_to(p), Point(1, 1).distance_to(Point(2, 2)))",
