   "xml_index": 6,
   "xml_name": "L11_006_Midpoint And Moving A Line",
   "display_name": "Midpoint And Moving A Line",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A method can <b>delegate</b> work to the objects it is made of: moving a line means moving both of its points, and <code>Point</code> already knows how to move.</p>\n<p>The <b>midpoint</b> of a line is the point halfway between its ends: <code>((x1 + x2) / 2, (y1 + y2) / 2)</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> add two methods to <code>Line</code>:</p>\n<ul><li><code>midpoint()</code> returns a <b>new</b> <code>Point</code> at the midpoint, with the line's colour;</li><li><code>move(dx, dy)</code> moves the whole line, by calling <code>move</code> on both points.</li></ul>\n<p>For example, <code>print(Line(Point(0, 0), Point(4, 2)).midpoint())</code> prints <code>(2.0, 1.0)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        return round(((other.x - self.x) ** 2 + (other.y - self.y) ** 2) ** 0.5, 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self]\n\n\nclass Line:\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2, color=\"black\"):\n        self.p1 = p1            # two Point objects\n        self.p2 = p2\n        self.color = color\n\n    def length(self):\n        return self.p1.distance_to(self.p2)\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.p1) + \"-\" + str(self.p2)\n\n    def midpoint(self):\n        # write your code here\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        # write your code here\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
