   "xml_name": "L11_007_Drawing A Line",
   "display_name": "Drawing A Line",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A line is drawn with <code>ax.plot</code>, giving the x values and the y values of its two ends:</p>\n<pre>ax.plot([x1, x2], [y1, y2], color=...)</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> add the methods <code>draw(ax)</code>, which draws the line with <code>ax.plot</code> in the line's colour, and <code>points()</code>, which returns the list <code>[p1, p2]</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, drawing <code>Line(Point(0, 0), Point(3, 4), \"blue\")</code> records <code>('plot', [0, 3], [0, 4], 'blue')</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        return round(((other.x - self.x) ** 2 + (other.y - self.y) ** 2) ** 0.5, 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self]\n\n\nclass Line:\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2, color=\"black\"):\n        self.p1 = p1            # two Point objects\n        self.p2 = p2\n        self.color = color\n\n    def length(self):\n        return self.p1.distance_to(self.p2)\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.p1) + \"-\" + str(self.p2)\n\n    def midpoint(self):\n        return Point((self.p1.x + self.p2.x) / 2, (self.p1.y + self.p2.y) / 2, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.p1.move(dx, dy)\n        self.p2.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        # write your code here\n\n    def points(self):\n        # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- See your drawing (practice site only; not graded) ----\n# Remove the # in front of the lines below, then press Pre-check.\n# (Put the # back before Check if Check becomes slow.)\n# import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n# fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n# ax.set_aspect('equal')\n# Line(Point(0, 0), Point(3, 4), \"blue\").draw(ax)\n# Line(Point(0, 4), Point(3, 0), \"red\").draw(ax)\n",
