  {
   "xml_index": 8,
   "xml_name": "L11_008_A Triangle Class",
   "display_name": "A Triangle Class",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A <code>Triangle</code> is made of three <code>Point</code> objects, its corners <code>a</code>, <code>b</code> and <code>c</code>. Its <b>perimeter</b> is the sum of its three side lengths.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> the classes <code>Point</code> and <code>Line</code> are given. Write the class <code>Triangle</code> whose constructor takes three points <code>a</code>, <code>b</code>, <code>c</code> and an optional <code>color</code> (default <code>\"black\"</code>), with the method <code>perimeter()</code> returning the sum of the three side lengths (a to b, b to c, c to a), rounded to 2 decimal places.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>Triangle(Point(0, 0), Point(3, 0), Point(0, 4)).perimeter()</code> returns <code>12.0</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        return round(((other.x - self.x) ** 2 + (other.y - self.y) ** 2) ** 0.5, 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self]\n\n\nclass Line:\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2, color=\"black\"):\n        self.p1 = p1            # two Point objects\n        self.p2 = p2\n        self.color = color\n\n    def length(self):\n        return self.p1.distance_to(self.p2)\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.p1) + \"-\" + str(self.p2)\n\n    def midpoint(self):\n        return Point((self.p1.x + self.p2.x) / 2, (self.p1.y + self.p2.y) / 2, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.p1.move(dx, dy)\n        self.p2.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.plot([self.p1.x, self.p2.x], [self.p1.y, self.p2.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self.p1, self.p2]\n\n\nclass Triangle:\n    def __init__(self, a, b, c, color=\"black\"):\n        # write your code here\n\n    def perimeter(self):\n        # write your code here\n",
