  {
   "xml_index": 9,
   "xml_name": "L11_009_Area With The Shoelace Formula",
   "display_name": "Area With The Shoelace Formula",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The area of a triangle with corners <code>(x1, y1)</code>, <code>(x2, y2)</code>, <code>(x3, y3)</code> can be computed directly from the coordinates with the <b>shoelace formula</b>:</p>\n<pre>area = | x1*(y2 - y3) + x2*(y3 - y1) + x3*(y1 - y2) | / 2</pre>\n<p>(<code>| ... |</code> means the absolute value: <code>abs(...)</code> in Python.) If the three points lie on one line, the area is 0.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> add the method <code>area()</code> to <code>Triangle</code>, returning the area rounded to 2 decimal places.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>Triangle(Point(0, 0), Point(4, 0), Point(0, 3)).area()</code> returns <code>6.0</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        return round(((other.x - self.x) ** 2 + (other.y - self.y) ** 2) ** 0.5, 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self]\n\n\nclass Line:\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2, color=\"black\"):\n        self.p1 = p1            # two Point objects\n        self.p2 = p2\n        self.color = color\n\n    def length(self):\n        return self.p1.distance_to(self.p2)\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.p1) + \"-\" + str(self.p2)\n\n    def midpoint(self):\n        return Point((self.p1.x + self.p2.x) / 2, (self.p1.y + self.p2.y) / 2, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.p1.move(dx, dy)\n        self.p2.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.plot([self.p1.x, self.p2.x], [self.p1.y, self.p2.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self.p1, self.p2]\n\n\nclass Triangle:\n    def __init__(self, a, b, c, color=\"black\"):\n        self.a = a              # three Point objects\n        self.b = b\n        self.c = c\n        self.color = color\n\n    def perimeter(self):\n        return round(self.a.distance_to(self.b) + self.b.distance_to(self.c) + self.c.distance_to(self.a), 2)\n\n    def area(self):\n        # write your code here\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(Triangle(Point(0, 0), Point(4, 0), Point(0, 3)).area())",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "6.0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(Triangle(Point(0, 0), Point(1, 1), Point(2, 2)).area())",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0.0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(Triangle(Point(1, 1), Point(4, 5), Point(-2, 7)).area())",
