  {
   "xml_index": 11,
   "xml_name": "L11_011_Moving And Scaling",
   "display_name": "Moving And Scaling",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Two ways to transform a triangle:</p>\n<ul><li><b>move</b>: shift every corner by <code>(dx, dy)</code> (delegate to the points' <code>move</code>);</li><li><b>scale</b> by a factor <code>k</code> about its center: each corner moves along the line from the center, to <code>center + k * (corner - center)</code>. With <code>k = 2</code> the triangle doubles in size; with <code>k = 0.5</code> it shrinks to half; the center stays where it is.</li></ul>\n<pre>new_x = cx + k * (x - cx)\nnew_y = cy + k * (y - cy)</pre>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> add the methods <code>move(dx, dy)</code> and <code>scale(k)</code> to <code>Triangle</code>. <code>scale</code> computes the center first (with <code>center()</code>), then changes each corner's <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> as above, rounding each new coordinate to 2 decimal places.</p>\n<p>For example, scaling <code>Triangle(Point(0, 0), Point(6, 0), Point(0, 3))</code> by <code>2</code> moves the corner <code>(6, 0)</code> to <code>(10.0, -1.0)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        return round(((other.x - self.x) ** 2 + (other.y - self.y) ** 2) ** 0.5, 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self]\n\n\nclass Line:\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2, color=\"black\"):\n        self.p1 = p1            # two Point objects\n        self.p2 = p2\n        self.color = color\n\n    def length(self):\n        return self.p1.distance_to(self.p2)\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.p1) + \"-\" + str(self.p2)\n\n    def midpoint(self):\n        return Point((self.p1.x + self.p2.x) / 2, (self.p1.y + self.p2.y) / 2, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.p1.move(dx, dy)\n        self.p2.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.plot([self.p1.x, self.p2.x], [self.p1.y, self.p2.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self.p1, self.p2]\n\n\nclass Triangle:\n    def __init__(self, a, b, c, color=\"black\"):\n        self.a = a              # three Point objects\n        self.b = b\n        self.c = c\n        self.color = color\n\n    def perimeter(self):\n        return round(self.a.distance_to(self.b) + self.b.distance_to(self.c) + self.c.distance_to(self.a), 2)\n\n    def area(self):\n        a, b, c = self.a, self.b, self.c\n        return round(abs(a.x * (b.y - c.y) + b.x * (c.y - a.y) + c.x * (a.y - b.y)) / 2, 2)\n\n    def center(self):\n        cx = round((self.a.x + self.b.x + self.c.x) / 3, 2)\n        cy = round((self.a.y + self.b.y + self.c.y) / 3, 2)\n        return Point(cx, cy, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        # write your code here\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        # write your code here\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
