  {
   "xml_index": 13,
   "xml_name": "L11_013_A Scene Of Shapes",
   "display_name": "A Scene Of Shapes",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A <code>Scene</code> holds a <b>list of shapes</b> of different kinds: points, lines and triangles. Because every shape class has its own <code>move(dx, dy)</code>, the scene can move everything with one loop, calling <code>move</code> on each shape without caring what kind it is (<b>polymorphism</b>, from Lab 10).</p>\n<div style=\"margin:6px 0 4px\"><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">scene : Scene</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\"><div style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px\">shapes = &#x27;[pt, line, tri]&#x27;</div></div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;padding:22px 8px 0 0;color:#8a939c\">&rarr;</div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">pt : Point</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\">&nbsp;</div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">line : Line</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\">&nbsp;</div></div><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #2a8c8c;border-radius:10px;margin:4px 10px 4px 0;min-width:120px;background:#eef7f7\"><div style=\"padding:3px 10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;color:#1d6464;border-bottom:1px solid #b9dcdc\">tri : Triangle</div><div style=\"padding:4px 10px\">&nbsp;</div></div></div>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> the classes <code>Point</code>, <code>Line</code> and <code>Triangle</code> are given. Write the class <code>Scene</code> whose constructor starts with an empty list <code>shapes</code>, with methods:</p>\n<ul><li><code>add(shape)</code> adds a shape to the list;</li><li><code>count()</code> returns the number of shapes;</li><li><code>move_all(dx, dy)</code> moves every shape.</li></ul>\n<p>For example, after adding a point and a line to an empty scene, <code>scene.count()</code> returns <code>2</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        return round(((other.x - self.x) ** 2 + (other.y - self.y) ** 2) ** 0.5, 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self]\n\n\nclass Line:\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2, color=\"black\"):\n        self.p1 = p1            # two Point objects\n        self.p2 = p2\n        self.color = color\n\n    def length(self):\n        return self.p1.distance_to(self.p2)\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.p1) + \"-\" + str(self.p2)\n\n    def midpoint(self):\n        return Point((self.p1.x + self.p2.x) / 2, (self.p1.y + self.p2.y) / 2, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.p1.move(dx, dy)\n        self.p2.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.plot([self.p1.x, self.p2.x], [self.p1.y, self.p2.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self.p1, self.p2]\n\n\nclass Triangle:\n    def __init__(self, a, b, c, color=\"black\"):\n        self.a = a              # three Point objects\n        self.b = b\n        self.c = c\n        self.color = color\n\n    def perimeter(self):\n        return round(self.a.distance_to(self.b) + self.b.distance_to(self.c) + self.c.distance_to(self.a), 2)\n\n    def area(self):\n        a, b, c = self.a, self.b, self.c\n        return round(abs(a.x * (b.y - c.y) + b.x * (c.y - a.y) + c.x * (a.y - b.y)) / 2, 2)\n\n    def center(self):\n        cx = round((self.a.x + self.b.x + self.c.x) / 3, 2)\n        cy = round((self.a.y + self.b.y + self.c.y) / 3, 2)\n        return Point(cx, cy, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        for p in (self.a, self.b, self.c):\n            p.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        c = self.center()\n        for p in (self.a, self.b, self.c):\n            p.x = round(c.x + k * (p.x - c.x), 2)\n            p.y = round(c.y + k * (p.y - c.y), 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        xs = [self.a.x, self.b.x, self.c.x]\n        ys = [self.a.y, self.b.y, self.c.y]\n        ax.fill(xs, ys, color=self.color, alpha=0.4)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self.a, self.b, self.c]\n\n\nclass Scene:\n    def __init__(self):\n        # write your code here\n\n    def add(self, shape):\n        # write your code here\n\n    def count(self):\n        # write your code here\n\n    def move_all(self, dx, dy):\n        # write your code here\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
