  {
   "xml_index": 14,
   "xml_name": "L11_014_Bounding Box",
   "display_name": "Bounding Box",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>To fit a picture on the screen, we need its <b>bounding box</b>: the smallest rectangle, with sides parallel to the axes, containing every point of every shape. It is given by the smallest and largest x and y values: <code>(min_x, min_y, max_x, max_y)</code>.</p>\n<p>Every shape has a method <code>points()</code> returning its points, so the scene can collect all the points of all its shapes in one loop, whatever kinds of shapes they are.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> add the method <code>bounding_box()</code> to <code>Scene</code>, returning the tuple <code>(min_x, min_y, max_x, max_y)</code> over all points of all shapes. The scene has at least one shape.</p>\n<p>For example, a scene with <code>Point(1, 5)</code> and <code>Line(Point(-2, 0), Point(3, 1))</code> has the bounding box <code>(-2, 0, 3, 5)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        return round(((other.x - self.x) ** 2 + (other.y - self.y) ** 2) ** 0.5, 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self]\n\n\nclass Line:\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2, color=\"black\"):\n        self.p1 = p1            # two Point objects\n        self.p2 = p2\n        self.color = color\n\n    def length(self):\n        return self.p1.distance_to(self.p2)\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.p1) + \"-\" + str(self.p2)\n\n    def midpoint(self):\n        return Point((self.p1.x + self.p2.x) / 2, (self.p1.y + self.p2.y) / 2, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.p1.move(dx, dy)\n        self.p2.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.plot([self.p1.x, self.p2.x], [self.p1.y, self.p2.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self.p1, self.p2]\n\n\nclass Triangle:\n    def __init__(self, a, b, c, color=\"black\"):\n        self.a = a              # three Point objects\n        self.b = b\n        self.c = c\n        self.color = color\n\n    def perimeter(self):\n        return round(self.a.distance_to(self.b) + self.b.distance_to(self.c) + self.c.distance_to(self.a), 2)\n\n    def area(self):\n        a, b, c = self.a, self.b, self.c\n        return round(abs(a.x * (b.y - c.y) + b.x * (c.y - a.y) + c.x * (a.y - b.y)) / 2, 2)\n\n    def center(self):\n        cx = round((self.a.x + self.b.x + self.c.x) / 3, 2)\n        cy = round((self.a.y + self.b.y + self.c.y) / 3, 2)\n        return Point(cx, cy, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        for p in (self.a, self.b, self.c):\n            p.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        c = self.center()\n        for p in (self.a, self.b, self.c):\n            p.x = round(c.x + k * (p.x - c.x), 2)\n            p.y = round(c.y + k * (p.y - c.y), 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        xs = [self.a.x, self.b.x, self.c.x]\n        ys = [self.a.y, self.b.y, self.c.y]\n        ax.fill(xs, ys, color=self.color, alpha=0.4)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self.a, self.b, self.c]\n\n\nclass Scene:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.shapes = []\n\n    def add(self, shape):\n        self.shapes.append(shape)\n\n    def count(self):\n        return len(self.shapes)\n\n    def move_all(self, dx, dy):\n        for s in self.shapes:\n            s.move(dx, dy)          # every shape has its own move()\n\n    def bounding_box(self):\n        # write your code here\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "s = Scene()\ns.add(Point(1, 5))\ns.add(Line(Point(-2, 0), Point(3, 1)))\nprint(s.bounding_box())",
