  {
   "xml_index": 16,
   "xml_name": "L11_016_Draw A House",
   "display_name": "Draw A House",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>To finish, use your classes to build a picture: a simple <b>house</b>.</p>\n<p>For a house at position <code>(x, y)</code> (its bottom-left corner) with size <code>s</code>, add these shapes to a new scene, <b>in this order</b>:</p>\n<ol><li>the walls: four <code>Line</code>s, colour <code>\"brown\"</code>: bottom <code>(x, y)</code>-<code>(x + s, y)</code>, right <code>(x + s, y)</code>-<code>(x + s, y + s)</code>, top <code>(x + s, y + s)</code>-<code>(x, y + s)</code>, left <code>(x, y + s)</code>-<code>(x, y)</code>;</li><li>the roof: a <code>Triangle</code> with corners <code>(x, y + s)</code>, <code>(x + s, y + s)</code>, <code>(x + s / 2, y + 1.5 * s)</code>, colour <code>\"red\"</code>;</li><li>a door: a <code>Point</code> at <code>(x + s / 2, y + s / 4)</code>, colour <code>\"black\"</code>.</li></ol>\n<p><b>Careful:</b> give every line its <b>own</b> new <code>Point</code> objects. If two lines shared one <code>Point</code> object, <code>move_all</code> would move that point twice (once for each line). This is aliasing again (Lab 7).</p>\n<p>Uncomment the drawing block at the bottom to see your house (and a second, bigger one next to it).</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> the classes <code>Point</code>, <code>Line</code>, <code>Triangle</code> and <code>Scene</code> are given. Write the function <code>make_house(x, y, s)</code> which returns the <code>Scene</code> described above.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>make_house(0, 0, 4).bounding_box()</code> returns <code>(0, 0, 4, 6.0)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "class Point:\n    def __init__(self, x, y, color=\"black\"):\n        self.x = x\n        self.y = y\n        self.color = color\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return \"(\" + str(self.x) + \", \" + str(self.y) + \")\"\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.x = self.x + dx\n        self.y = self.y + dy\n\n    def distance_to(self, other):\n        return round(((other.x - self.x) ** 2 + (other.y - self.y) ** 2) ** 0.5, 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.scatter([self.x], [self.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self]\n\n\nclass Line:\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2, color=\"black\"):\n        self.p1 = p1            # two Point objects\n        self.p2 = p2\n        self.color = color\n\n    def length(self):\n        return self.p1.distance_to(self.p2)\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return str(self.p1) + \"-\" + str(self.p2)\n\n    def midpoint(self):\n        return Point((self.p1.x + self.p2.x) / 2, (self.p1.y + self.p2.y) / 2, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        self.p1.move(dx, dy)\n        self.p2.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        ax.plot([self.p1.x, self.p2.x], [self.p1.y, self.p2.y], color=self.color)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self.p1, self.p2]\n\n\nclass Triangle:\n    def __init__(self, a, b, c, color=\"black\"):\n        self.a = a              # three Point objects\n        self.b = b\n        self.c = c\n        self.color = color\n\n    def perimeter(self):\n        return round(self.a.distance_to(self.b) + self.b.distance_to(self.c) + self.c.distance_to(self.a), 2)\n\n    def area(self):\n        a, b, c = self.a, self.b, self.c\n        return round(abs(a.x * (b.y - c.y) + b.x * (c.y - a.y) + c.x * (a.y - b.y)) / 2, 2)\n\n    def center(self):\n        cx = round((self.a.x + self.b.x + self.c.x) / 3, 2)\n        cy = round((self.a.y + self.b.y + self.c.y) / 3, 2)\n        return Point(cx, cy, self.color)\n\n    def move(self, dx, dy):\n        for p in (self.a, self.b, self.c):\n            p.move(dx, dy)\n\n    def scale(self, k):\n        c = self.center()\n        for p in (self.a, self.b, self.c):\n            p.x = round(c.x + k * (p.x - c.x), 2)\n            p.y = round(c.y + k * (p.y - c.y), 2)\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        xs = [self.a.x, self.b.x, self.c.x]\n        ys = [self.a.y, self.b.y, self.c.y]\n        ax.fill(xs, ys, color=self.color, alpha=0.4)\n\n    def points(self):\n        return [self.a, self.b, self.c]\n\n\nclass Scene:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.shapes = []\n\n    def add(self, shape):\n        self.shapes.append(shape)\n\n    def count(self):\n        return len(self.shapes)\n\n    def move_all(self, dx, dy):\n        for s in self.shapes:\n            s.move(dx, dy)          # every shape has its own move()\n\n    def bounding_box(self):\n        pts = []\n        for s in self.shapes:\n            pts = pts + s.points()\n        xs = [p.x for p in pts]\n        ys = [p.y for p in pts]\n        return (min(xs), min(ys), max(xs), max(ys))\n\n    def draw(self, ax):\n        for s in self.shapes:\n            s.draw(ax)              # each shape draws itself\n\n\ndef make_house(x, y, s):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- See your drawing (practice site only; not graded) ----\n# Remove the # in front of the lines below, then press Pre-check.\n# (Put the # back before Check if Check becomes slow.)\n# import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n# fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n# ax.set_aspect('equal')\n# make_house(0, 0, 4).draw(ax)\n# h = make_house(6, 0, 6)\n# h.draw(ax)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "class FakeAx:  # records drawing calls instead of drawing\n    def __init__(self): self.calls = []\n    def scatter(self, xs, ys, **kw): self.calls.append(('scatter', list(xs), list(ys), kw.get('color')))\n    def plot(self, xs, ys, **kw): self.calls.append(('plot', list(xs), list(ys), kw.get('color')))\n    def fill(self, xs, ys, **kw): self.calls.append(('fill', list(xs), list(ys), kw.get('color')))\nax = FakeAx()\nmake_house(0, 0, 4).draw(ax)\nfor c in ax.calls:\n    print(c)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "('plot', [0, 4], [0, 0], 'brown')\n('plot', [4, 4], [0, 4], 'brown')\n('plot', [4, 0], [4, 4], 'brown')\n('plot', [0, 0], [4, 0], 'brown')\n('fill', [0, 4, 2.0], [4, 4, 6.0], 'red')\n('scatter', [2.0], [1.0], 'black')",
